CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --unwind 4 --object-bits 11 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ by-ref capture observes the live entity: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ by-ref capture modifies the referenced entity: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ mixed by-copy snapshot and by-reference live: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[expr.prim.lambda.capture]: an entity captured by reference is captured as a
reference member of the closure that denotes the entity.  Lambda rework Phase C
lowers an explicit-by-reference capture to a reference member bound to the
entity at capture time, so the closure observes the live entity and can modify
it through the reference (also in a const/non-mutable lambda).  Mixed by-copy
(snapshot) and by-reference (live) captures are exercised.
